  "description": "Built to go flat out. Downhill bikes are made to conquer the roughest terrain, steepest gradients, and biggest jumps — and the Nukeproof Dissent Carbon was born for it. With 200mm of travel front and rear, it’s ready for anything from your local woods to Morzine or Whistler — built to get you down fast, smooth, and in one piece. The Dissent has 'dropped in' at RedBull Rampage and stood on the podium at RedBull Hardline and World Cup Downhills, it's been proven on the toughest terrain in the world to make a better bike for everyone. The Triple Clamp DH fork and rear shock deliver buttery-smooth suspension feel, while simple DH gearing and powerful brakes keep things reliable when the trail gets wild. Whether you’re shredding laps with your mates, slapping on a race plate, or sending the biggest gaps, the Dissent Carbon has your back.",
